// E0311: a name whose pieces are not all words. `fb_w` says nothing to a reader
// who did not write it; `framebuffer_width` does. Every identifier the program
// declares is split on `_` and each piece looked up in the vocabulary (./state.id),
// which bin/idc loads from data/words/ only under --word-scan: with no
// vocabulary loaded the scan does nothing, so no ordinary build is affected.
//
// It covers functions, parameters and locals, exported names and conf.id
// constants, struct names and their fields, and the names of the program's
// files and directories (./pathscan.id). A name is judged once however many functions declare it, and the
// scan ends with one line of totals (names judged, names not spelled in words).

word_scan() {
  if((import vocab_count)[0] > 0) {
    vocab_run();
  }
} return void;
